author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 210
acceptance_criteria: "The declared dependency-kind domain names exactly one canonical spelling per relation, and every current spelling remains accepted as a hidden alias, proven by a test over the full pre-change spelling set; Write-time canonicalization is uniform: any accepted alias is stored as its canonical kind, extending the single depends_on to blocked_by case shipped under pm-fl0c to the whole domain, so no new alias row can be created; Item type words are no longer accepted as relationship kinds, or the decision to keep them is recorded with the relation each one denotes; pm graph audit and the deps surfaces disclose alias rows still present in stored data as a named legacy count rather than folding them silently into the canonical bucket; The declared canonical set and its alias map are readable from the contracts surface, so a grep or jq pipeline can be written against a documented vocabulary instead of an observed one; Existing alias rows on terminal items are left unmutated; their remediation stays with pm-hnc9w7"
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: 85
resolution: Canonical registry-driven writes with explicit legacy alias observability
expected_result: Every accepted alias stores one canonical kind while historical terminal rows remain untouched and discoverable
actual_result: Create/update canonicalize all built-in aliases; contracts publishes ontology; deps and graph audit emit legacy alias counts; tests and manual compiled CLI acceptance pass
